  "aiContextParagraph": "Gold market trends in Indonesia show consistent price fluctuations for various brands, including Antam and those available through the state-owned pawnbroker Pegadaian. On November 20, 2026, reports confirmed that Antam gold reached a price of Rp2.5 million per gram, representing an Rp11,000 decrease from previous levels. Simultaneously, the buyback price—the value offered to individuals selling their gold back—saw a significant drop of Rp78,000. These price movements follow a period of declining gold values observed throughout mid-November. While the gold sector faces downward market pressure, other industrial commodities like nickel have reported price increases during the same month. PT Aneka Tambang Tbk continues to manage its mining operations and sustainability initiatives as these market shifts impact both retail investors and the broader domestic precious metals industry.",
